>>Speaking of etc:
>>	(1) A blessed ring of teleport control
>>		With intrinsic teleport, you have a means of quick escape
>>		and instant travel!  Also a quick way to escape being
>>		swallowed, death by drowning (if lucky), and a great way to
>>		un-satiate yourself very quickly for intrinsic gaining.
> 
> 	Why would anyone want to wish for this?  I could understand
> polymorph control but teleport control?  If you're a wizard you get that
> intrinsic automagically.  If you'r not you can always kill a tengu.
> 
For a good reason: if you are lawful most tengus will be friendly, so
killing them is not recommended. Besides, the probability of gaining tele
contr. from a corpse is quite low - usually you'll have to find several
tengus before you get the intrinsic - a ring is a sure and lawful way.

For the poster of the original question: don't listen to people giving
you lists with nicely ordered wishes... it depends very much on the
character you are playing, your playing style and tactical situation. 
I, for one, very seldom ask for arifact weapon as my first wish - even if
I get the wish very early in the game.

 A few interesting wishes nobody seems to have mentioned before:

blessed ring of searching (for characters that don't gain the intrinsic - 
invaluable for avoiding nasty traps and locating magic portals)
blessed spellbook of identify
blessed spellbook of fireball
blessed spellbook of charm monster (you'll learn to value these once on
yor way back, when you get occasionally surrounded by nasties).

